---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro'
---

<Page
  title="Mortar privacy policy"
  description="What the Mortar app and its browser extension send over the network, to whom, and when."
  heading="Privacy policy"
  lede="Mortar has no account system, no analytics, no telemetry and no server that collects anything about you. It talks only to the services below, and only for the reason given."
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Privacy', href: '/privacy/' }]}
>
<h2>What Mortar sends, and to whom</h2>
<div class="table-wrap">
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Service</th>
        <th>When</th>
        <th>What it receives</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Nexus Mods (nexusmods.com)</td>
        <td>
          When you sign in, browse, download or check for mod updates
        </td>
        <td>
          Your Nexus API key or sign-in token, and the ids of the mods and
          files involved. Nexus's own
          <a href="https://help.nexusmods.com/article/18-privacy-policy"
            >privacy policy</a
          >
          applies.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>GitHub (github.com, api.github.com)</td>
        <td>
          When Mortar checks for its own updates, and for mods hosted on
          GitHub
        </td>
        <td>
          A request for the latest release of Mortar or of that mod. No
          account, no mod list.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>SMAPI (smapi.io)</td>
        <td>
          When Mortar checks the mods in a profile for updates and
          compatibility
        </td>
        <td>
          The ids and versions of the installed mods, the same request
          SMAPI itself makes when the game starts.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>SMAPI log parser (smapi.io/log)</td>
        <td>Only when you choose to share a game log and confirm</td>
        <td>That SMAPI log, which lists your mods and may include folder paths with your user name. smapi.io gives back a link you can share.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Stardew mod dataset (raw.githubusercontent.com)</td>
        <td>When Mortar looks up mod metadata</td>
        <td>A request for public data files; nothing about you.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Steam CDN (cdn.cloudflare.steamstatic.com)</td>
        <td>When Mortar shows a game's cover art</td>
        <td>A request for that game's public image.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Your own network</td>
        <td>Only when you send a profile to another computer</td>
        <td>
          The profile, and its mod files when both computers use the same
          Nexus account.
        </td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
<p>
  A share link carries your profile in the part after <code>#</code>,
  which browsers never send to a server, so opening one on
  mortar.rethunk.tech does not reveal the profile to this site.
</p>

<h2>What stays on your computer</h2>
<p>
  Profiles, settings, logs, crash reports and save backups stay in
  Mortar's data folder. Your Nexus key is kept in your system keyring.
  Report a Mortar bug collects diagnostics into a file and opens a GitHub
  issue form; nothing is sent until you submit that issue yourself.
</p>

<h2>Browser extension</h2>
<p>
  The extension talks only to Mortar on your own computer. Its policy is
  on the
  <a href="/extension/#privacy">extension page</a>.
</p>

<h2>Discord bot</h2>
<p>
  The Mortar bot in Mortar's Discord server has its own
  <a href="/bot/privacy/">privacy policy</a> and
  <a href="/bot/terms/">terms</a>.
</p>

<h2>This website</h2>
<p>
  mortar.rethunk.tech is a static site with no cookies. It counts visits
  with <a href="https://plausible.io/data-policy">Plausible</a>, which
  keeps no personal data: no cookies, no IP addresses, and nothing that
  follows you to other sites.
  The downloads page asks GitHub's public API for the latest release so it
  can show file sizes. Game pictures on the game pages load from Steam's
  image servers, with no referrer sent. The hosting provider keeps
  standard access logs.
</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>
  Questions about privacy:
  <a href="mailto:legal@rethunk.tech">legal@rethunk.tech</a>. Security reports:
  <a href="mailto:opensource@rethunk.tech">opensource@rethunk.tech</a>.
</p>
</Page>
